course: dictionary
lesson: 1068
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Use the words around it to find the right one. «A bouncy ball squashes and springs back, while clay squashes and stays squashed.» Here bouncy means it springs back up well after it is pressed or dropped.
explain: Bouncy can also describe a person or animal who is lively, cheerful and full of energy. A bouncy puppy is never still for long. Bouncy hair means hair that is full and springy.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «A limerick is a funny five-line poem with a bouncy rhythm.» A poem cannot spring back like a ball, so bouncy means the beat has a lively swing. Try "lively" in the sentence, and it still makes sense.
fact: Bouncy means springing back up well after being pressed or dropped.
fact: Bouncy can also mean lively, cheerful and full of energy, for a person or an animal.
fact: Bouncy hair is full and springy.
fact: Bouncy has two other forms: bouncier and bounciest.
fact: Scientists test which balls are bounciest: they drop each ball from the same height and measure the bounce, so the test is fair.
exercise: «A bouncy ball squashes and springs back, while clay squashes and stays squashed.» What does bouncy mean here? | Full of colour | *Springs back up well | Stays squashed flat | Very heavy
exercise: Which meaning of bouncy describes a puppy that runs round the garden all day? | Springs back when dropped | *Lively, cheerful and full of energy | Full and springy | Quiet and still
exercise: In a fair test of bouncy balls, what must stay the same? | The name painted on each ball | The time of day you eat lunch | The shape of the room | *The height you drop each ball from
test: «A limerick is a funny five-line poem with a bouncy rhythm.» In a poem, what does bouncy mean? | Very quiet and slow | *Lively, with a swing to the beat | Full of holes | Made of rubber
test: «Leah sneaked off to the bouncy castle in her turn to help.» What is a bouncy castle? | A bouncing sort of cake | A stone tower on a hill | A kind of tall tree | *A large inflatable you jump about on
exam: Which meaning of bouncy fits a happy, energetic child best? | Stays squashed | Full and springy | Springs back when dropped | *Lively, cheerful and full of energy
